@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="aivs-page">
    <div class="aivs-page-header">
        <h1 class="aivs-page-title">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
        <div class="aivs-page-subtitle">
            How the Attribute Inspection &amp; Verification System handles information.
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="aivs-panel">
        <h2 class="aivs-panel-title">What this system is for</h2>
        <p>
            AIVS is an internal system used by the City of Johannesburg to route, assign,
            inspect, and verify property valuation attribute records submitted through the
            City's valuation processes. Access is limited to authorised sector managers,
            valuers, and executive staff.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="aivs-panel">
        <h2 class="aivs-panel-title">Information processed in AIVS</h2>
        <p>
            In the course of an attribute review, AIVS may process property and contact
            information supplied as part of a valuation submission, including property
            descriptions and identifiers, declared property attributes, representative and
            contact details, inspection scheduling information, and files or evidence
            uploaded in support of a review.
        </p>
        <p>
            This information is used strictly to assign, inspect, and verify property
            valuation attributes, and to maintain an audit trail of decisions made during
            that process.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="aivs-panel">
        <h2 class="aivs-panel-title">Access and retention</h2>
        <p>
            Access to records in AIVS is restricted by role — sector managers, valuers, and
            executives see only the records relevant to their sector or assignment. All
            actions taken on a record (assignment, review, scheduling, submission) are
            logged for audit purposes.
        </p>
        <p>
            Information held in AIVS is retained in line with the City of Johannesburg's
            records management and Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA)
            obligations.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="aivs-panel">
        <h2 class="aivs-panel-title">Questions</h2>
        <p>
            If you have a question about how your information is used in AIVS, or believe
            your account does not have the correct level of access, contact your sector
            manager or the AIVS system administrator.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
